1
00:00:00,022 --> 00:00:05,308
Resgrid Relay listens to an audio feed,
detects configured tones, records

2
00:00:05,314 --> 00:00:10,279
dispatch audio, and creates calls for the
associated department or groups.

3
00:00:10,446 --> 00:00:14,725
It can help departments connect an
existing paging process when they cannot

4
00:00:14,744 --> 00:00:17,254
modify the upstream dispatch system.

5
00:00:18,053 --> 00:00:21,491
The recording plan begins with an approved
sample audio feed

6
00:00:21,491 --> 00:00:23,252
and known tone frequencies.

7
00:00:23,473 --> 00:00:28,396
Check the input signal, configure the
intended recording behavior, and review

8
00:00:28,398 --> 00:00:30,523
the department or group recipients.

9
00:00:30,719 --> 00:00:34,495
Verify the exact installer and interface
against the supported

10
00:00:34,495 --> 00:00:36,388
Relay release before capture.

11
00:00:37,163 --> 00:00:38,939
Use synthetic test audio.

12
00:00:39,116 --> 00:00:44,339
Inspect the resulting call, the captured
recording, and the intended recipients.

13
00:00:44,583 --> 00:00:48,336
Test nonmatching tones separately and
document what was observed.

14
00:00:48,485 --> 00:00:53,412
The public Relay installation page
contains incomplete older steps, so it

15
00:00:53,414 --> 00:00:57,783
is a feature reference rather than a
verified modern installation procedure.

16
00:00:58,558 --> 00:01:02,855
Retain the synthetic audio fixture,
selected release, approved

17
00:01:02,891 --> 00:01:05,787
configuration, and observed test result.

18
00:01:06,003 --> 00:01:09,014
A recorder will need the supported Relay
application and

19
00:01:09,016 --> 00:01:12,642
an audio test setup to turn this briefing
into a live walkthrough.

